<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!-- The first FrontEnd UI setup channel the project spent a day concluding did
     not exist.

     Three settings have never applied on this install — MapScript, Leader and
     MapSeed — and all three failed for one reason: the mod tried to reach the
     setup screen with `<AddUserInterfaces><Context>FrontEnd</Context>`, and
     NOTHING SHIPPED USES THAT. Across 38 shipped DLC, `AddUserInterfaces`
     appears in `InGameActions` nine times and in `FrontEndActions` zero times.
     Every InGame hook this mod has works; the single FrontEnd hook never did,
     which is the `setup: "(absent)"` in every seat event.

     What shipped DLC DO use in FrontEndActions is `<UpdateDatabase>` — and the
     Create Game screen is driven by the CONFIGURATION DATABASE, not by Lua. So
     the setup defaults are reachable as data.

     ⚠ WHY EVERY GAME WAS CONTINENTS. `Base/Assets/Configuration/Data/SetupParameters.xml`
     ships TWO rows for the Map parameter, differing only in which modes they
     support:

       DefaultValue="Continents.lua"  SupportsSinglePlayer=1  LAN/Internet/HotSeat=0
       DefaultValue="Pangaea.lua"     SupportsSinglePlayer=0  LAN/Internet/HotSeat=1

     Pangaea was ALREADY the default — for multiplayer. Single player gets
     Continents. The game was doing exactly what its data said, and asking for
     Pangaea through a channel it never read.

     This matters because on Continents a seat can start alone: 21 of 43 runs
     past turn 60 (49%) NEVER met another civilization, so no war target, no
     captured capital, no domination — and score is unreachable at ~5:1 behind.
     Half of all runs were unwinnable from the map draw.

     ⚠ Matched on DefaultValue rather than on SupportsSinglePlayer, because that
     names exactly the one row to change and cannot accidentally match the
     multiplayer row (which is already Pangaea) if the flags are ever edited. -->
<GameInfo>
	<Parameters>
		<Update>
			<Where ParameterId="Map" DefaultValue="Continents.lua"/>
			<Set>
				<DefaultValue>Pangaea.lua</DefaultValue>
			</Set>
		</Update>
		<!-- Seed probe only. Both rows are Domain="int" and ship with no
		     DefaultValue. `tools/civ6_seed_check.py` established that writing them
		     through this configuration database does NOT reach world generation:
		     identical requests still produced different capitals, maps and civs.

		     Keep the writes solely to test a future claim that the game has gained a
		     working seed channel. They must not support a static plan or a paired
		     real-Civ6 result until that probe passes. MapRandomSeed writes
		     Map/RANDOM_SEED; GameRandomSeed writes GAME_SYNC_RANDOM_SEED.

		     `CIVVIS_SEED` is substituted by install.py. A literal 0 reads as unset. -->
		<Update>
			<Where ParameterId="MapRandomSeed"/>
			<Set>
				<DefaultValue>CIVVIS_SEED</DefaultValue>
			</Set>
		</Update>
		<Update>
			<Where ParameterId="GameRandomSeed"/>
			<Set>
				<DefaultValue>CIVVIS_SEED</DefaultValue>
			</Set>
		</Update>
	</Parameters>
</GameInfo>
